type3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat8\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth2835\clcbpatraw8\cellx2835\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat8\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth1417\clcbpatraw8\cellx4252\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat8\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth5670\clcbpatraw8\cellx9922\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat8\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth567\clcbpatraw8\cellx10489\row}\pard\ltrpar\qj\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 The full wording of hazard (H) phrases is given in section 16 of the sheet.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par\ltrrow}\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899  }{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs22\cf1\insrsid4669103 SECTION 4. First aid measures}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\cell}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\row}\pard\ltrpar\qj\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\insrsid4669103 4.1. Description of first aid measures\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 In case of doubt or in the presence of symptoms contact a doctor and show him this document.\par In case of more severe symptoms, ask for immediate medical aid.\par EYES: Remove, if present, contact lenses if the situation allows you to do so easily. Wash immediately with plenty of water for at least 15 minutes, opening the eyelids fully. Get medical advice/attention.\par SKIN: Take off contaminated clothing. Wash immediately and thoroughly with running water (and soap if possible). Get medical advice. Avoid further contact with contaminated clothing.\par INGESTION: Do not induce vomiting unless explicitly authorised by a doctor. Do not give anything by mouth to an unconscious person. Get medical advice/attention.\par INHALATION: Remove victim to fresh air, away from the accident scene. Get medical advice/attention.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\ul\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Rescuer protection\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 It is good practice for rescuers lending support to a person who has been exposed to a chemical substance or to a mixture to wear personal protective equipment. The nature of such protection depends on the hazard level of the substance or mixture, on the type of exposure and on the extent of the contamination. In the absence of other more specific indications, use of disposable gloves in the event of possible contact with body fluids is recommended. For the type of PPE suitable for the characteristics of the substance or mixture, see section 8.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 4.2. Most important symptoms and effects, both acute and delayed\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Specific information on symptoms and effects caused by the product are unknown.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 DELAYED EFFECTS: Based on the information currently available, there are no known cases of delayed effects following exposure to this product.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 4.3. Indication of any immediate medical attention and special treatment needed\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 If symptoms occur, whether acute or delayed, consult a doctor.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\ul\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Means to have available in the workplace for specific and immediate treatment\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Running water for skin and eye wash.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par\par\ltrrow}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899  }{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs22\cf1\insrsid4669103 SECTION 5. Firefighting measures}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\cell}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\row}\pard\ltrpar\qj\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\insrsid4669103 5.1. Extinguishing media\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\insrsid4669103 SUITABLE EXTINGUISHING EQUIPMENT\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Extinguishing substances are: carbon dioxide, foam, chemical powder. For product loss or leakage that has not caught fire, water spray can be used to disperse flammable vapours and protect those trying to stem the leak.\par UNSUITABLE EXTINGUISHING EQUIPMENT\par Do not use jets of water. Water is not effective for putting out fires but can be used to cool containers exposed to flames to prevent explosions.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 5.2. Special hazards arising from the substance or mixture\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 HAZARDS CAUSED BY EXPOSURE IN THE EVENT OF FIRE\par Excess pressure may form in containers exposed to fire at a risk of explosion. Do not breathe combustion products.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 5.3. Advice for firefighters\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 GENERAL INFORMATION\par Use jets of water to cool the containers to prevent product decomposition and the development of substances potentially hazardous for health. Always wear full fire prevention gear. Collect extinguishing water to prevent it from draining into the sewer system. Dispose of contaminated water used for extinction and the remains of the fire according to applicable regulations.\par SPECIAL PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT FOR FIRE-FIGHTERS\par Normal fire fighting clothing i.e. fire kit (BS EN 469), gloves (BS EN 659) and boots (HO specification A29 and A30) in combination with self-contained open circuit positive pressure compressed air breathing apparatus (BS EN 137).\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par\par\ltrrow}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899  }{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs22\cf1\insrsid4669103 SECTION 6. Accidental release measures}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\cell}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\row}\pard\ltrpar\qj\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 6.1. Personal precautions, protective equipment and emergency procedures\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Block the leakage if there is no hazard.\par Wear suitable protective equipment (including personal protective equipment referred to under Section 8 of the safety data sheet) to prevent any contamination of skin, eyes and personal clothing. These indications apply for both processing staff and those involved in emergency procedures.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Send away individuals who are not suitably equipped. Use explosion-proof equipment. Eliminate all sources of ignition (cigarettes, flames, sparks, etc.) from the leakage site.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 6.2. Environmental precautions\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 The product must not penetrate into the sewer system or come into contact with surface water or ground water.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 6.3. Methods and material for containment and cleaning up\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Collect the leaked product into a suitable container. Evaluate the compatibility of the container to be used, by checking section 10. Absorb the remainder with inert absorbent material.\par Make sure the leakage site is well aired. Contaminated material should be disposed of in compliance with the provisions set forth in point 13.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 6.4. Reference to other sections\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Any information on personal protection and disposal is given in sections 8 and 13.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par\par\ltrrow}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899  }{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs22\cf1\insrsid4669103 SECTION 7. Handling and storage}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\cell}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\row}\pard\ltrpar\qj\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\insrsid4669103 7.1. Precautions for safe handling\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Keep away from heat, sparks and naked flames; do not smoke or use matches or lighters. Without adequate ventilation, vapours may accumulate at ground level and, if ignited, catch fire even at a distance, with the danger of backfire. Avoid bunching of electrostatic charges. When performing transfer operations involving large containers, connect to an earthing system and wear antistatic footwear. Vigorous stirring and flow through the tubes and equipment may cause the formation and accumulation of electrostatic charges. In order to avoid the risk of fires and explosions, never use compressed air when handling. Open containers with caution as they may be pressurised. Do not eat, drink or smoke during use. Avoid leakage of the product into the environment.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 7.2. Conditions for safe storage, including any incompatibilities\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Store only in the original container. Store the containers sealed, in a well ventilated place, away from direct sunlight. Store in a cool and well ventilated place, keep far away from sources of heat, naked flames and sparks and other sources of ignition. Keep containers away from any incompatible materials, see section 10 for details.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Storage class TRGS 510 (Germany):\par 3\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 7.3. Specific end use(s)\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\insrsid4669103 Information not available\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\insrsid4669103\par\ltrrow}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899  }{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs22\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 SECTION 8. Exposure controls/personal protection}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\cell}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\row}\pard\ltrpar\qj\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par\ltrrow}