er with face and eye wash station.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 HAND PROTECTION\par Protect hands with category III work gloves.\par The following should be considered when choosing work glove material (see standard EN 374): compatibility, degradation, permeability time.\par The work gloves' resistance to chemical agents should be checked before use, as it can be unpredictable. The gloves' wear time depends on the duration and type of use.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 SKIN PROTECTION\par Wear category I professional long-sleeved overalls and safety footwear (see Regulation 2016/425 and standard EN ISO 20344). Wash body with soap and water after removing protective clothing.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 Consider the appropriateness of providing antistatic clothing in the case of working environments in which there is a risk of explosion.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 EYE PROTECTION\par Wear airtight protective goggles (see standard EN ISO 16321).\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 RESPIRATORY PROTECTION\par Respiratory protection devices must be used if the technical measures adopted are not suitable for restricting the worker's exposure to the threshold values considered. Use a mask with a type A filter whose class (1, 2 or 3) must be chosen according to the limit of use concentration. (see standard EN 14387).\par If the substance considered is odourless or its olfactory threshold is higher than the corresponding TLV-TWA and in the case of an emergency, wear open-circuit compressed air breathing apparatus (in compliance with standard EN 137) or external air-intake breathing apparatus (in compliance with standard EN 138). For a correct choice of respiratory protection device, see standard EN 529.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\f1\fs16\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 ENVIRONMENTAL EXPOSURE CONTROLS\par The emissions generated by manufacturing processes, including those generated by ventilation equipment, should be checked to ensure compliance with environmental standards.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\par\par\par\ltrrow}\trowd\irow0\irowband0\lastrow\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph70\trleft0\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind70\tblindtype3\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrtbl\clbrdrl\brdrtbl\clbrdrb\brdrtbl\clbrdrr\brdrtbl\clcbpat19\cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth10773\clcbpatraw19\cellx10773\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899  }{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\b\f1\fs22\cf1\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899 SECTION 9. Physical and chemical properties}{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\cell}\pard\ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0{\rtlch\fcs1\af0\ltrch\fcs0\lang2057\langfe1040\langnp2057\insrsid4669103\charrsid5988899\trowd\irow0\irowban